WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Good to meet you, man.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.960
Good to meet you, sir.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.880
All right, so I kind of want to start

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.800
at the basics or the foundation.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:07.640
I want to see what-

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.460
Can I just check?

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.300
Yes.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.140
Are you a fascist?

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:10.960
No.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.800
Okay.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.560
I describe myself as, I think, just a Christian.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.380
Fair enough.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.480
I'm a devout Christian.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.320
Good to hear.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.639
So, I want to start, like, what is your connection

00:00:19.639 --> 00:00:23.480
to the Constitution and why do you love it so much?

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.639
Like, what makes it so important that Trump

00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:28.280
would defy something like the Constitution to you personally?

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.280
Great questions.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.120
My first connection is I'm an American citizen.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.759
I naturalized American citizen.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.480
Took a pledge to this country, to the Constitution.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.799
As a previous speaker has said,

00:00:38.799 --> 00:00:39.799
Constitution's not perfect.

00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:40.799
A lot of things I don't like about it.

00:00:40.799 --> 00:00:42.799
I don't like the Second Amendment.

00:00:42.799 --> 00:00:43.639
There's various amendments.

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:45.240
I don't like the way the Senate is set up.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.400
I'm sure there's things you don't like

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.480
about the Constitution.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.919
The difference is, I don't think you can just

00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:51.439
illegally defy the Constitution.

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:52.400
I don't think each and everyone

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.439
is going to make up whatever we want.

00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:56.639
Certainly presidents who are elected with an oath, right?

00:00:56.639 --> 00:00:58.639
Donald Trump took an oath to preserve, protect,

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.720
and defend the Constitution.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.240
And now when he's asked on television,

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.639
isn't it your job to uphold the Constitution?

00:01:02.639 --> 00:01:06.040
He said on NBC, I don't know, which goes against his oath.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.760
And I'm identifying specific amendments

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:08.599
where he is violating.

00:01:08.599 --> 00:01:10.000
He's only six months into his presidency

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
defying the First Amendment, the Fourth Amendment,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.879
the Fifth Amendment, the 14th Amendment.

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:15.360
He wants to defy the 22nd Amendment

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.680
and be president for a third term.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.000
This is the problem we have right now.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.239
Free speech is under assault.

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:21.639
The free press is under assault.

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:23.519
Due process is under assault.

00:01:23.519 --> 00:01:24.559
The right to be in your home

00:01:24.559 --> 00:01:26.040
and not be invaded by federal agents,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.760
the Fourth Amendment, is under assault.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.239
So that, for me, is a problem.

00:01:29.239 --> 00:01:30.160
Okay.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.519
Well, I'd like to start to say

00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:34.320
I really don't find the Constitution that important.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.400
I find it to be like a 300-year-old document.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.559
And it was created to defy the country

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:44.559
that subjugated your ancestors in India.

00:01:44.559 --> 00:01:47.879
And then your parents probably moved from India to Britain.

00:01:47.879 --> 00:01:50.080
And then you move here to tell us

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.239
that we should listen to a piece of paper

00:01:52.239 --> 00:01:55.480
that you were never even connected to to begin with.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.720
So I want to say, like, if I don't care about it,

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.559
why do you care about it so much?

00:02:00.559 --> 00:02:01.800
How do you run a country

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.839
without any kind of laws or due process?

00:02:03.839 --> 00:02:05.080
And by the way, you do care about it,

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.120
because without the First Amendment,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.040
you wouldn't be sitting here.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.520
Oh, I agree with the First Amendment.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.119
So do you agree with Donald Trump's crackdown

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:11.360
on the First Amendment?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.080
He's imprisoning people for their speech.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.360
He's threatening free speech media organizations.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.960
He's threatening peaceable assembly.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.240
These are all rights under the First Amendment.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.240
Why aren't you bothered by that

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.080
as a conservative who claims to love the First Amendment?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.160
So I actually, I don't like the First Amendment.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.240
I like free speech.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.199
The First Amendment is what guarantees free speech.

00:02:27.199 --> 00:02:28.440
I'm from the UK, by the way.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.199
I'm from the UK, which is a democracy.

00:02:30.199 --> 00:02:31.360
We don't have the First Amendment.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.360
No, because that's one of the things

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.320
I do like about the Constitution.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:34.679
I wish the UK did have a First Amendment.

00:02:34.679 --> 00:02:35.679
I'm a journalist.

00:02:35.679 --> 00:02:38.039
Arrested for praying outside abortion clinics

00:02:38.039 --> 00:02:39.160
and stuff like that, right?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.880
So you're opposed to people

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.679
being arrested for speech crimes, I assume.

00:02:42.679 --> 00:02:43.600
It depends what it is.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.440
If it's like the people-

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.039
Oh, so you're like one of the previous speakers.

00:02:46.039 --> 00:02:47.199
As long as it's someone who agrees with you,

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:48.039
you don't mind the crackdown.

00:02:48.039 --> 00:02:48.880
No, no, no, I support-

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.479
Either we consistently support principles or we don't.

00:02:50.479 --> 00:02:51.759
I support free speech 100%.

00:02:51.759 --> 00:02:52.600
Okay.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.960
So do you think Donald Trump

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:54.880
is defying the Constitution

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.960
by cracking down on the First Amendment?

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.720
So I think he's cracking down on free speech

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.199
like the deportation of Mahmoud Khalil, who's-

00:03:02.199 --> 00:03:03.520
Who was just released from prison by a judge

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.199
saying his First Amendment rights were violated.

00:03:05.199 --> 00:03:06.520
And I agree with the judge

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.559
and I disagree with Trump deporting them.

00:03:08.559 --> 00:03:10.279
But I think that's more a matter of free speech

00:03:10.279 --> 00:03:12.240
and not the Constitution.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.559
I think that's pedantry at this moment.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.399
I think you've conceded

00:03:14.399 --> 00:03:15.639
that he is cracking down on free speech,

00:03:15.639 --> 00:03:16.639
which is the First Amendment.

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:17.880
So he is defying the Constitution.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.240
So it's a pleasure to be in agreement with you, sir.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.199
All right, pause.

00:03:21.199 --> 00:03:22.639
You've been voted out by the majority.

00:03:22.679 --> 00:03:23.520
Please return to your seats.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.360
All right, thank you very much.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.199
Thank you.

00:03:25.199 --> 00:03:26.039
Thank you.

